# Altimeter Trig Calculation Simulation
# TRIG6 Model: Height measurement via trigonometric angles
# θ = altitude phase, R = accuracy, D = wind drift, N = instrument noise
# Danger: steep angle tan∞ (error amplification)

# Initial configuration
set eq 1.0
theta pi/4  # Balanced angle (45 degrees)
alpha 0.2
theta_opt pi/6  # Optimal angle for accuracy (30 degrees)

# Step 1: Initial measurement
step
state  # Expected: R=0.85 (high accuracy), D=0.15 (wind), N=0.2 (calibration), danger=No

# Step 2: Correct for drift if detected
if drift > 0.3 then theta pi/3  # Adjust to 60 degrees
step
state  # Expected: Converged R=0.92

# Final state: High accuracy altimeter reading achieved
# Fitness: f = R*(1-D)*(1-N)*eq
